> In this case your best strategy is to make shortish visits to the Bigroom
> level, staying on the stairs. Whenever you manage to kill some adjacent
> monster, check your Hp. If it's not at the maximum value or close to it,
> climb upstairs to heal until the Hp is back at the maximum value again.
> And while downstairs, keep a close look at the Hp value, and retreat
> upstairs if it gets low.

An interesting option: If you think you are going to go through a lot
of cycles up and down the stairs you might consider alternating
between killing the meanest monster in the crowd near you and
taking a lot of damage before retreating upstairs, with killing one of
the easier monsters in the crowd near you and having only a little
damage before retreating.  Doing that thins the crowd a little faster.
You don't want to focus on the weakest one each time because
that approach ends up distilling down to the worst of the bunch
towards the end, but focusing on the strongest only allows the
weaker ones to hit you a lot of times before they die.  Basically,
once you descend think over which one you want to handle on
this cycle and have a reason for that choice.

> And while healing yourself at the Oracle level, it may be a good idea not
> to stay at the stairs going down, but go near to the stairs going up.
> That way you can climb further up to heal better, if some monster gets
> created that is tough for your weakened conditiion.

Excellent.



